            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p><b>Ingredients</b></p><p><br></p><p>1 teaspoon Smoky Mountains Cowboy Chai blend (lapsang souchong, assam, cinnamon, ginger, green cardamom, cloves, star anise, and black pepper)</p><p><br></p><p>1 cup water</p><p><br></p><p>1 tablespoon honey or maple syrup (optional, adjust to your sweetness preference)</p><p><br></p><p>1/4 cup fresh orange juice (adds a zesty contrast to the deep spices)</p><p><br></p><p>1-2 slices of fresh orange (for garnish)</p><p><br></p><p>1 cinnamon stick (for garnish)</p><p><br></p><p>A pinch of smoked sea salt (optional, for an extra touch of smokiness)</p><p><br></p><p><b>Instructions</b></p><p><br></p><p><b>Boil the Tea:</b> Start by bringing 1 cup of water to a boil in a small saucepan. Once boiling, add your Smoky Mountains Cowboy Chai blend. Let the tea simmer for about 5-7 minutes, depending on how strong you like your brew. The longer it steeps, the more intense the smoky and spicy flavors will be.</p><p><br></p><p><b>Strain and Sweeten:</b> After steeping, strain the tea into your favorite mug. Stir in honey or maple syrup to taste, depending on how sweet you want your drink.</p><p><br></p><p><b>Add Orange Juice:</b> Pour in 1/4 cup of fresh orange juice. The citrus helps brighten the drink, cutting through the richness of the spices and creating a refreshing balance with the smoky flavor.</p><p><br></p><p><b>Garnish and Serve:</b> Garnish your drink with a slice of fresh orange and a cinnamon stick. This adds a beautiful touch of color, aroma, and even more spice to your drink. For an extra layer of flavor, consider sprinkling a tiny pinch of smoked sea salt on top. This subtle touch enhances the smokiness and adds a unique twist to the brew.</p><p><br></p><p><b>Enjoy:</b> Now, take a moment to savor the layers of smoky, spicy, and citrusy goodness in your warm cup. It’s the perfect beverage to enjoy while unwinding after a long day or sharing with friends during a cozy gathering.</p></div>
            </div>
            
            
          </div>
        

